  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>→</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> be strictly increasing function such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Then, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow></munder><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to"
  },
